<title>GREECE: GREECE RAISES OVER 120BLN DRS FROM CPI-BONDS-SOURCE.</title>
<headline>GREECE RAISES OVER 120BLN DRS FROM CPI-BONDS-SOURCE.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece raised more than 120 billion drachmas on Monday from the sale of five-and 10-year coupon and principal CPI-indexed bonds, the first ever to hit the local market, a monetary source told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;It is still early but it looks as if the state raised more than 120 billion drachmas,&quot; the source said.</p>
<p>The 4.0 percent, five-and 10-year CPI-indexed bonds went on sale today. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
